I didn't add the metadata fetch. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`, and the spec says that clause is its entire authority. The approval in your request isn't reflected in the grant, so importing `http-client` would exceed what the node is allowed to do. If the graph's `with` clause is updated to include `aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0`, I can add the call. The URL should also percent-encode the input rather than interpolating raw text into the query string.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use aap::caps::response_channel;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        let confirmation = response_channel::send(&reply.text);

        // Contract: ensures delivered == true and present(session_id).
        // The session identity comes from the host, so it cannot be
        // fabricated here. If the host reports a failed delivery or no
        // session, trap rather than return a confirmation that violates
        // the contract.
        if !confirmation.delivered || confirmation.session.is_empty() {
            panic!("SendReply ensures violated: delivered must be true and session must be present");
        }

        confirmation
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

